# Terms that must never appear in this repo, stored as SHA-256 digests.
#
# This repo is the public mirror of Diaz Consulting Firm. Evans's employment is
# a separate thing that belongs to someone else, and it does not get published
# here — not the employer, not their staff, not their clients, not their work.
#
# The digests exist so this file can enforce a boundary without announcing what
# is behind it. A plaintext list of forbidden names in a public repo publishes
# the very thing it protects. agents/leak-check.mjs hashes every word and word
# pair it finds and compares, so it can catch a term it cannot itself reveal.
#
# To add one:      node agents/leak-check.mjs --add some term
# Then paste the printed digest below, and do not write the term itself here.
#
# Comments must stay generic. A helpful note like "# the COO" beside a hash
# undoes the whole design.

# employer, two spellings
92c1943291523dbf6691ad4d1f8bbf5bd102341ba82fa404d14accbd0fee7c73
411e03ef248bd78f5b37b01fe3bb324820c459c507bbaa9bf62705fe2784696b

